    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0549" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/260b.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As soon as Colonel Gorgas arrives you will cooperate with him in every possible
                    proper way. The Chargé d’Affaires of Ecuador here informs the Department that
                    his Government desires bids from American firms upon the bases of sanitation to
                    be reported by Colonel Gorgas. The Department learns that a reputable American
                    firm will at the proper time present a comprehensive proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
